.TH NP_PROCESSOR 3 "June 2026" "netpipe v0.1.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
np_processor_fn, np_processor_tcp_stream, np_processor_rate_limit, np_processor_payload_transform, np_processor_flow_tracker, np_processor_lua, np_processor_tls_decrypt, np_pipeline_add_processor \- netpipe packet processors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netpipe.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef np_err_t (*np_proc_fn)(np_packet_t *" pkt ", void *" userdata ");"
.PP
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_fn(np_proc_fn " fn ", void *" userdata ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_tcp_stream(void);"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_rate_limit(uint64_t " bytes_per_sec ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_payload_transform(const char *" mode ", const char *" pattern ", const char *" replacement ");"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_flow_tracker(void);"
.br
.BI "np_processor_t *np_processor_lua(const char *" script_path ");"
.br
.BI "NP_EXPERIMENTAL np_processor_t *np_processor_tls_decrypt(const char *" keylog_path ");"
.br
.BI "np_err_t np_pipeline_add_processor(np_pipeline_t *" pl ", np_processor_t *" proc ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions create and attach packet processors or transforms to a pipeline.
Processors inspect, modify, rate-limit, decrypt, or track packets as they flow through the pipeline.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_fn ()
function creates a custom callback-based processor.
Whenever a packet passes through this stage, the user-defined callback function
.I fn
is executed with a pointer to the packet and the user-supplied
.IR userdata .
The callback must return
.B NP_OK
to allow the packet to proceed, or a negative
.B np_err_t
to filter out the packet or indicate a pipeline error.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_tcp_stream ()
function creates a TCP stream reassembly processor.
It tracks TCP handshakes and sequence numbers to reconstruct application-layer
payloads.
The reassembler implements:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 3
Per-flow, per-direction reassembly contexts keyed on the 4-tuple.
.IP \(bu 3
Sorted segment queue with overlap clipping for retransmissions.
.IP \(bu 3
Hole-timeout flushing (1 second default) for gap recovery.
.IP \(bu 3
SYN/FIN/RST state machine with re-SYN detection (connection reuse).
.IP \(bu 3
RFC 793 sequence arithmetic (correct across 2^32 wrap-around).
.RE
.PP
Reassembled payload bytes are attached to the packet as
.I pkt->stream_data
(of length
.IR pkt->stream_len ),
enabling deep packet inspection of application protocols (like HTTP and TLS).
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_rate_limit ()
function creates a Token Bucket rate limiter that throttles the pipeline's
throughput to the specified
.IR bytes_per_sec .
It uses
.BR nanosleep (2)
for high-resolution timing and handles oversized packets gracefully
(packets larger than the rate cap are passed through with a warning).
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_payload_transform ()
function creates a payload replacer/transformer.
It searches for a specific byte or string
.I pattern
in the packet payload and replaces it with
.IR replacement .
The parameter
.I mode
can define regex or literal substitution modes.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_flow_tracker ()
function creates a flow tracking processor.
It maps packets to bi-directional conversations (flows) based on the five-tuple
(source/destination IP, source/destination port, protocol) and assigns unique
flow IDs.
Includes automatic garbage collection of idle flows (60 second timeout,
sweep every 1024 packets).
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_lua ()
function loads and executes an external Lua script specified by
.I script_path
for every packet.
The script registers callbacks via
.BR NP_REGISTER_PROCESSOR() :
an
.I init()
function (called once at startup), a
.I process(pkt)
function (called per packet \(em return
.B false
to drop the packet), and a
.I free()
function (called at shutdown).
This allows writing dynamic packet manipulation or analysis logic in Lua.
.PP
The
.BR np_processor_tls_decrypt ()
function
.RB ( NP_EXPERIMENTAL )
creates a TLS session decryption processor.
It loads an NSS key-log file
.RI ( SSLKEYLOGFILE
format) from
.I keylog_path
and decrypts TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 traffic inline.
.PP
Supported cipher suites:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 3
TLS 1.3:
.IR TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR TLS_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR TLS_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
.IP \(bu 3
TLS 1.2 (GCM/ChaCha20):
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR RSA_WITH_AES_128_GCM_SHA256 ,
.IR RSA_WITH_AES_256_GCM_SHA384 ,
.IR ECDHE_RSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256 ,
.IR ECDHE_ECDSA_WITH_CHACHA20_POLY1305_SHA256
.RE
.PP
Supported key-log record types:
.IR CLIENT_RANDOM ,
.IR CLIENT_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET ,
.IR SERVER_HANDSHAKE_TRAFFIC_SECRET ,
.IR CLIENT_TRAFFIC_SECRET_0 ,
.IR SERVER_TRAFFIC_SECRET_0 .
.PP
Decrypted plaintext is placed in
.I pkt->stream_data
and the TLS layer's
.I data
pointer is redirected to the plaintext, so downstream processors that walk
.I pkt->layers[]
see the decrypted bytes.
.PP
The
.BR np_pipeline_add_processor ()
function attaches a processor to the pipeline.
Processors are executed sequentially in the order they are added.
Processors added to a pipeline are owned by the pipeline and automatically freed when
.BR np_pipeline_free ()
is called.
.SH RETURN VALUES
Processor creation functions return a pointer to a newly allocated
.B np_processor_t
on success, or
.B NULL
on failure.
.PP
.BR np_pipeline_add_processor ()
returns
.B NP_OK
on success, or a negative
.B np_err_t
code on failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS TCP stream reassembly
.nf
np_pipeline_t *pl = np_pipeline_new();
np_pipeline_add_processor(pl, np_processor_tcp_stream());
np_pipeline_add_source(pl, np_source_file("capture.pcap"));
np_pipeline_add_sink(pl, np_sink_json(stdout));
np_pipeline_run(pl);
np_pipeline_free(pl);
.fi
.SS TLS decryption
.nf
np_pipeline_t *pl = np_pipeline_new();
np_pipeline_add_processor(pl, np_processor_tls_decrypt("/tmp/keys.log"));
np_pipeline_add_source(pl, np_source_file("tls_capture.pcap"));
np_pipeline_add_sink(pl, np_sink_json(stdout));
np_pipeline_run(pl);
np_pipeline_free(pl);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libnetpipe (3),
.BR np_pipeline (3),
.BR np_packet (3),
.BR netpipe (1)
